  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe tool Properties page, before (main) and after (this PR):\n\n| Before | After |\n|---|---|\n| ![End mill tool page on main](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FlamingFireCoding/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr-2663-endmill-before.png) | ![End mill tool page with the property grid](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FlamingFireCoding/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr-2663-endmill-after.png) |\n\nThe waterjet nozzle page, before (main) and after (this PR):\n\n| Before | After |\n|---|---|\n| ![Waterjet nozzle page on main](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FlamingFireCoding/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr-2663-waterjet-before.png) | ![Waterjet nozzle page with the property grid](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FlamingFireCoding/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr-2663-waterjet-after.png) |\n\n- The tool Properties page is a label-left property grid: one row per\n  setting, label left, input right.\n- Four collapsible groups: Geometry, Holder, Cutting data, Catalog.\n- New file `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tool_settings_grid.rs` holds the grid.\n  `tool_settings.rs` loses its long stack of paragraphs.\n- The inline help paragraphs are hover tooltips on the row labels.\n- The grid group header is the only header. The waterjet recipe and the\n  catalog rows do not open a second, nested header.\n- The waterjet recipe Feed row is a feed row: `num_feed_row` in\n  `fields.rs` shows the `mm/min` / `in/min` suffix and the feed\n  precision in both document unit modes.\n- Main's #2016 holder-reference display law is kept inside the grid's\n  `holder()` rows: holder diameter and length name the library entry\n  instead of two typed fields. The merge grafted that law into the grid.\n\nNo command changed. Every edit still rides the same Apply / Add commands,\nso one edit is one undoable `ChangeTool`.\n\n## Readings\n\n- `docs/decisions/2014-tool-property-grid.md` - what was chosen and dropped.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/tool_properties.rs`: the groups, the\n  labels, the label-left order and the fold.\n- `waterjet_recipe_feed_row_reads_as_a_feed_rate_in_both_unit_modes`\n  (in `waterjet_recipe.rs`): the recipe feed reads `731 mm/min` in\n  millimetre units and `28.78 in/min` in inch units, and no recipe\n  field shows the feed as a plain length.\n- `layout_page_tool` (in `page_layout.rs`) names the new Geometry header.\n- The #2016 pair in `tool_holder_reference.rs` passes on the new grid:\n  `a_library_holder_sizes_the_holder_fields_until_its_outline_is_edited`\n  and `the_profile_tab_names_the_entry_and_the_picker_shows_it`. The\n  picker test hovers the Profile tab before its click: egui hit-tests a\n  press with the previous frame, and the grid settles the window size\n  over its first frames.\n- Structural, edm_tool_visibility, waterjet_recipe and ball_corner tests\n  follow the new row layout.\n\n## Gate\n\n- `camcraft-ui` lib tests on this head: 1250 passed, and 4 failures in\n  the `frame_cost_probe` tests (`frame_cost_probe.rs:278`, \"the area\n  preview is filled\"). Those 4 are the known machine-dependent #2766\n  reds: a stash test on the branch head without this fix fails the\n  same 4, and the reviewer's runs on this PR show them green.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets`: clean.\n- The diff touches `camcraft-ui` only; no other crate's tests apply.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Tooltip hover by a real mouse: the structural tests assert labels and\n  commands, not hover painting.\n- The tool editor window in the theme live lane; it runs only at a cut.\n\nChangelog: The tool Properties show a label-left property grid in four collapsible groups.\n\nFixes #2014\n",
